(a) the major agreements and MoUs signed during the India-Australia summit, including the key outcomes of the Joint Declaration on Defence and Security Cooperation;
(b) the progress made in Comprehensive Economic Cooperation Agreement (CECA) negotiations and the outcomes relating to critical minerals and clean energy cooperation;
(c) the key initiatives under the India-Australia Defence Innovation Corridor, including measures to enhance defence cooperation and interoperability; and
(d) the follow-up mechanism and roadmap for implementing the summit outcomes, including the expanded defence partnership?

(a) the key initiatives and achievements under India's chairmanship of the Indian Ocean Rim Association (IORA);
(b) the outcomes of the India–Australia search and rescue training conducted at Chennai;
(c) the measures taken and roadmap envisaged to strengthen maritime security and cooperation among IORA member States; and
(d) the duration of India's Chairmanship and the roadmap for its successful transition?

(a) the key milestones achieved by India in meeting its Nationally Determined Contributions (NDCs) ahead of schedule;
(b) the major sectors that contributed to this achievement;
(c) the roadmap for India's next generation of more ambitious NDC targets; and
(d) the international recognition and significance of India's achievement in global climate action?

(a) the steps taken to integrate Artificial Intelligence (AI) into the national skilling ecosystem through the Skill India Digital Hub, National Centres of Excellence for Skilling and the ITI Upgradation Scheme;
(b) whether Ministry proposes a national framework for AI-based skill mapping and workforce profiling, including for informal sector;
(c) the number of AI, machine learning and data science qualifications notified under National Skill Qualification Framework (NSQF) and the candidates trained, certified and placed during the last three years, State-wise/UT-wise, including Odisha; and
(d) the measures taken and the roadmap envisaged to expand AI-enabled skilling in aspirational districts, tribal areas and rural regions?

(a) the State-wise and gender-wise progress achieved under the Pradhan Mantri Jan Dhan Yojana (PMJDY) and Jan Suraksha Schemes, including the cumulative number of beneficiaries as of June 2026;
(b) the total credit disbursed under the Pradhan Mantri MUDRA Yojana (PMMY), including the category-wise distribution among SC, ST, OBC and women entrepreneurs;
(c) the measures taken to ensure the quality and sustainability of MUDRA lending, including the trend in non-performing assets (NPAs); and
(d) the progress made under the Tarun Plus category, including the number and value of loans sanctioned and its contribution towards supporting growth-oriented micro enterprises?

(a) the key features of the e-Jagriti platform, including the legacy systems integrated into it and the AI/ML-enabled and accessibility features introduced for consumers, adjudicating authorities, senior citizens and persons with disabilities;
(b) the recognition and awards received by the platform for promoting digital governance and consumer justice;
(c) the progress made in operationalising e-Jagriti across the States, Union Territories and the National Consumer Disputes Redressal Commission (NCDRC); and
(d) the impact of the platform on the timely disposal of consumer complaints, including whether any State Consumer Commissions or the NCDRC have recorded monthly disposal exceeding fresh filings?

(a) the number of rainwater harvesting structures created under the Catch the Rain campaign since its inception and during 2025–26, along with the State-wise break-up;
(b) whether any scientific assessment has been undertaken to evaluate the campaign's impact on groundwater recharge, the districts showing significant improvement in groundwater levels and whether the findings have informed its next phase;
(c) the proportion of Jal Jeevan Mission (JJM) schemes incorporating rainwater harvesting or groundwater recharge structures for source sustainability; and
(d) the measures taken to enhance citizen participation in the Catch the Rain campaign?

(a) the number of Amrit Sarovars completed to date, their current operational status and the major achievements of the Mission;
(b) the measures taken to ensure their long-term maintenance and community participation through Panchayats and local institutions; and
(c) whether any assessment has been undertaken to evaluate the impact of Amrit Sarovars on groundwater recharge, water conservation and rural livelihoods and if so, the details thereof?

(a) the number of sellers, including MSMEs and small retailers, onboarded on the Open Network for Digital Commerce (ONDC), State-wise;
(b) the growth in transaction volumes and the key milestones achieved on the network since its inception; and
(c) the measures taken to promote ONDC, including outreach, capacity building and onboarding support extended to MSMEs and small retailers across the States and the roadmap for further expanding the network?

(a) the key features and outcomes of the Shaastraarth initiative introduced at Nalanda University's convocation and its role in promoting India's ancient knowledge traditions;
(b) the number of students, including international students and their countries of origin, who participated in the initiative;
(c) the measures taken and the roadmap envisaged to encourage similar debate and dialogue-based pedagogic traditions in Central Universities and other higher educational institutions; and
(d) the financial and institutional support extended to Nalanda University for implementing this initiative and promoting India's civilisational heritage in higher education?

(a) the number of schools, volunteers and organisations associated with the Vidyanjali programme during the last one year, along with the key achievements of the initiative;
(b) the framework and guidelines governing CSR and NGO participation under the programme;
(c) whether any assessment has been undertaken to evaluate the impact of Vidyanjali and Building as Learning Aid (BaLA) interventions on learning outcomes and the school environment; and
(d) the measures taken and the roadmap envisaged to expand these interventions, particularly in educationally backward districts?

(a) the key achievements of the Ministry since its establishment in July, 2021 and the major milestones envisaged under its five-year roadmap;
(b) the number of cooperative institutions and members benefitting from the Ministry's initiatives;
(c) the major reforms and initiatives undertaken in sectors such as dairy, logistics, mobility and renewable energy through the cooperative model; and
(d) the measures taken and the institutional mechanism established to ensure effective implementation of these initiatives in coordination with the States?

(a) the current status of the integration of AYUSH services into Ayushman Arogya Mandirs (AAMs), including policy guidelines or operational directives issued for integration and the timeline for full implementation;
(b) the number of AAMs and other public health facilities that currently offer AYUSH OPD services, State-wise;
(c) the types of AYUSH services (Yoga therapy, Ayurveda consultations, Naturopathy treatments, etc.) being provided at these centres;
(d) the measures taken to ensure quality, accreditation, training of AYUSH practitioners deployed at these centres and any monitoring and evaluation mechanisms in place; and
(e) the budgetary allocation and funding mechanism supporting integration of AYUSH into AAMs?

(a) the scale, outreach and key achievements of Ayurveda Day 2025, including the theme adopted and public participation across the country;
(b) the number of States/UTs that organised Ayurveda Day programmes and the major activities undertaken as part of the observance; and
(c) the measures taken and the roadmap envisaged to further institutionalise Ayurveda Day as a nationwide movement for preventive healthcare and public awareness?

(a) the transmission infrastructure augmentation undertaken to evacuate the rising wind and solar capacity in the country;
(b) the quantum of renewable power curtailed due to grid constraints during 2025-26;
(c) the steps taken/proposed to enhance grid flexibility, battery energy storage systems and renewable energy integration; and
(d) whether Government has prepared a roadmap for strengthening Green Energy Corridors and expanding transmission capacity to support the renewable energy targets by 2030 and if so, the details thereof?

(a) the extent to which the restructured PM SVANidhi Scheme has improved credit sustainability, repeat borrowing behaviour and income stability of beneficiaries, based on post-loan monitoring data;
(b) the status of uptake and utilisation of UPI-linked RuPay Credit Cards, including transaction patterns and challenges faced by street vendors; and
(c) the details of any roadmap prepared to strengthen grievance redressal, digital literacy and inclusion of newly identified vendors under the expanded coverage?

(a) the district-wise break-up of the package and the progress of component projects, including the Jakhapura-Jajpur Keonjhar Road-Baitarani Road and Hindol Road-Meramandali multi-tracking projects;
(b) the progress of the Bhubaneswar and Puri railway station redevelopment projects against the November, 2026 completion target; and
(c) the compensation-disbursal support extended to families affected by land acquisition for these projects?

(a) the key areas of cooperation outlined in the India–Japan Joint Vision for the Next Decade adopted in August 2025;
(b) the manner in which these initiatives are expected to support India’s economic engagement with the Global South;
(c) the framework developed for capacity building, skill development and industry collaboration; and 
(d) the manner in which the Joint Vision seeks to enhance people-to-people engagement and State Prefecture level cooperation between the two countries during the coming decade?

(a) the number of adolescent girls who have completed training and started income-generating activities under the Nurturing Aspirations through Vocational Training for Young Adolescent Girls (NAVYA) pilot;
(b) the criteria adopted for selection of 27 pilot districts and whether Odisha has been included, or is under consideration for inclusion, in the pilot; and
(c) the number of Industrial Training Institutes upgraded and the number of youth trained and placed under the Pradhan Mantri Kaushal Vikas Yojana in Odisha during 2025–26, along with the timeline for expansion of the NAVYA pilot to other districts?

(a) the historic digital automation completed across Primary Agricultural Credit Societies (PACS) via a Unified National Software platform in 2025;
(b) the cold-storage and warehouse capacities added through grassroot cooperative networks to eliminate middleman margins;
(c) the export volumes safely handled on behalf of small farmers by the newly established Multi-State Cooperative Export Society; and
(d) the block-level digital auditing models deployed to ensure complete financial transparency across rural credit lines?

(a) the reduction in the average time taken for disposal of consumer complaints through e-Jagriti as compared to the pre-digitisation period;
(b) the increase in consumer complaint filings from rural districts since the launch of e-Jagriti; and
(c) the measures taken to facilitate assisted filing for consumers with limited digital access?

(a) the cargo-handling capacity added at Paradip Port during 2025-26 and the improvement in turnaround time for bulk carriers; 
(b) the progress of last-mile rail and road connectivity projects under Sagarmala linking Paradip Port to Odisha's mineral and industrial belt; and 
(c) the investment approved for inland-waterways development along Odisha’s coastline?

(a) the current deployment status of AI and IoT-enabled components across Central Warehousing Corporation (CWC) facilities mapped on the Smart Warehousing Ecosystem dashboard;
(b) the total volume and value of credit loans disbursed to farmers against electronic Negotiable Warehouse Receipts (e-NWRs) through the e-Kisan Upaj Nidhi portal;
(c) whether the Credit Guarantee Scheme for pledge financing has successfully increased bank onboarding; and
(d) if so, the details thereof?

(a) category-wise details of the quantity of coal offered and actually allocated under the various components of the SHAKTI policy during the year 2025;
(b) extent to which coal linkages allocated under the SHAKTI policy have resulted in the operationalisation of power generation capacity, along with the capacity so commissioned;
(c) eligibility criteria and timelines prescribed for allocation of coal linkages under the revised SHAKTI policy;
(d) measures taken to improve participation in coal linkage auctions and ensure optimal utilisation of domestic coal resources; and
(e) revenue realised under the revised SHAKTI policy vis-à-vis the earlier allocation regime?

(a) the key outcomes of the India AI Impact Summit 2026 held in New Delhi, including the adoption of the New Delhi Declaration on AI Impact endorsed by 91 countries and international organisations;
(b) the progress in expansion of sovereign compute capacity under the IndiaAI Mission, including the addition of 20,000 Graphics Processing Units (GPUs) to the 38,000 already provisioned; 
(c) the steps being taken to support indigenous foundational models; and
(d) whether any AI compute or data centre investments are proposed in Odisha, if so, the details thereof?

(a) the measures undertaken to promote India as a tourism destination in domestic and international markets;
(b) the steps being taken to promote niche tourism segments such as MICE tourism and wedding tourism;
(c) the initiatives undertaken to strengthen tourist safety, promote digital tourism services and technology-enabled visitor facilitation, and improve ease of travel and affordability for domestic and international tourists;
(d) the manner in which citizen-engagement platforms are contributing to tourism awareness; and
(e) whether Government has assessed the impact of these initiatives on tourist footfall, visitor satisfaction and overall growth of the tourism sector and if so, the details thereof?

(a) the total number of Eklavya Model Residential Schools (EMRSs) sanctioned, functional and under construction in Odisha, district-wise;
(b) the steps taken to address shortage of teaching and non-teaching staff in functional EMRS in the State, particularly in Mayurbhanj, Sundargarh, Koraput and Malkangiri districts;
(c) whether any review has been conducted of academic outcomes of EMRS students in Odisha;
(d) if so, the details thereof;
(e) whether the scheme is proposed to be expanded to additional Scheduled Tribe-populated blocks in the State; and
(f) if so, the details and timeline thereof?

(a) the implementation status of the Integrated Aqua Park at Basantapur, Sambalpur sanctioned at a cost of ?100 crore under the Pradhan Mantri Matsya Sampada Yojana (PMMSY);
(b) the progress of the wholesale fish market project at Pandara, Bhubaneswar sanctioned at ?59.13 crore;
(c) the measures being taken to extend the Kisan Credit Card facility to the fishers of Odisha and to strengthen the value chain from production to marketing; and
(d) the details thereof?

(a) the total number of Health and Wellness Centres/Ayushman Arogya Mandirs operationalised in Odisha against the target, district-wise;
(b) the range of services, including Non-Communicable Disease (NCD) screening, being provided at these centres in tribal and remote blocks;
(c) whether shortage of doctors, paramedical staff or essential medicines has been reported from any of these centres in the State;
(d) if so, the details and steps taken to address the shortage;
(e) whether the impact of these centres on reducing patient load on district and tertiary hospitals in Odisha has been assessed; and
(f) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the details of increase in private hospital empanelment under Ayushman Bharat Pradhan Mantri - Jan Arogya Yojana (AB-PMJAY) since Jan 2023 to May 2026;
(b) the corresponding increase in private hospital empanelment under AB-PMJAY since Jan 2023 to May 2026 in Tier-II and Tier-III cities and aspirational districts;
(c) the data comparing female hospitalisation rates under AB PM-JAY with pre-2018 public health insurance schemes, State-wise; and
(d) the growth data on Ayushman Bharat Health Account (ABHA) creation, year-wise?

(a) whether any regional mineral processing park or Centre of Excellence on Critical Minerals is proposed to be set up in Odisha under the National Critical Mineral Mission;
(b) if so, the details, location and investment envisaged;
(c) the steps being taken to encourage downstream value-addition, such as ferro-alloy and steel processing, within the State rather than the export of raw ore;
(d) whether Odisha's existing steel and alloy industry has been factored into the site-selection criteria for such facilities, and;
(e) whether any assessment has been made of the employment likely to be generated from such processing infrastructure; and
(f) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the objectives and key features of the Skill India Digital Hub (SIDH) integrating skilling, certification and employment services, along with total budget allocation and expenditure so far;
(b) the progress in onboarding training providers, assessment agencies, employers and candidates nationwide, with State-wise registration and course data; and
(c) outcomes achieved in improving access to skill development, transparent certification and placement of youth in employment or apprenticeships, including measurable indicators?

(a) the specific targets set for Greenfield Expressway construction for the remainder of the fiscal year 2025-26;
(b) how the Ministry is utilising the InvIT mechanism to monetise highway assets and generate new capital post-August, 2025;
(c) whether a new policy has been adopted to accelerate land acquisition by streamlining the compensation process;
(d) the progress on the implementation of the Satellite-Based Toll Collection System (SBTC) on major corridors; and
(e) the manner in which the Ministry promoting the use of recycled materials like plastic and fly ash in road construction?

(a) whether Government proposes to establish a Digital Public Infrastructure Coordination Council (DPICC) for coordinated governance across Digital Public Infrastructure (DPI) ecosystems;
(b) the details of the proposed structure, mandate and functions of the Council;
(c) whether Central Government Ministries, regulators and sectoral DPI entities have been identified for representation;
(d) the names and details of such Ministries, regulators and entities; and
(e) whether the Council will conduct periodic Regulatory Impact Assessments of legal and regulatory frameworks governing DPIs, if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether the Ministry, in collaboration with the Ministry of Civil Aviation, has initiated any specialised programmes for drone pilot training and related skills under initiatives such as Drone Shakti and Namo Drone Didi;
(b) whether Government has sent any target for certified drone pilots and technicians to be trained by 2025 and the current progress made towards achieving these targets; and
(c) the steps taken to ensure affordable access to drone training for rural and semi-urban youth, including financial assistance or incentives?

(a) the milestones of 'Ayush Suraksha' Portal in tracking adverse drug reactions (ADRs) and misleading advertisements and complaints resolved across States/UTs;
(b) the status of collaboration with Department of Bio Technology (DBT) under BioE3 Policy for Ayu-genomics integration into precision medicine and progress of AyurTech Centre of Excellence at IIT Jodhpur;
(c) the steps taken by National Medicinal Plant Board (NMPB) for linking medicinal plant farmers with Green Credit Program and incentives for cultivating Arjuna and Guggal through carbon markets;
(d) the progress of Sowa-Rigpa wellness centres under Vibrant Villages Programme and NISR's medical camps in border tribal areas; and
(e) the Ministry's support for Organ-on-a-Chip and 3D-Bioprinting for AYUSH product validation and regulatory roadmap?

