(a) whether a national assessment has been commissioned estimating incremental water and peak power demand from (Artificial Intelligence) AI ready data centres over the next five to ten years, including disaggregated figures for major clusters;
(b) whether the Ministry proposes to mandate sustainability benchmarks, including water usage effectiveness limits, minimum recycled water usage and cooling-technology standards, with timelines and enforcement mechanisms; and
(c) whether an inter-Ministerial task force involving Ministries of Jal Shakti, Power, Environment and State Governments is proposed to integrate water-risk assessment into approvals, ensure community safeguards and link incentives to mandatory monitoring and public disclosure?

(a) the measures being taken to ensure that small and marginal farmers in Odisha benefit from AI-driven advisory services under Project Virtually Integrated System to Access Agricultural Resources (VISTAAR), if so, the details thereof;
(b) whether there are plans to integrate Project VISTAAR with other agricultural digital platforms in Odisha to enhance efficiency, if so, the details thereof;
(c) the manner in which the project is addressing region-specific agricultural challenges in Odisha, particularly in climate resilience and crop diversification; and
(d) the steps being taken to facilitate farmer training and capacity building programs to maximise the impact of Project VISTAAR?

(a) whether ISRO is pursuing further orbital docking experiments after the SPADEX mission;
(b) if so, the details of upcoming docking missions planned;
(c) how this capability would support India’s Gaganyaan and future space station programmes;
(d) whether academic institutions and national laboratories are involved in these docking technology developments; and
(e) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the objectives and key features of the revamped Rashtriya Gram Swaraj Abhiyan (RGSA) being implemented during the last five years;
(b) the total financial outlay of the scheme along with the year-wise funds released to States and Union Territories during the last five years;
(c) whether any evaluation or review mechanism has been instituted to assess the performance of the revamped scheme and if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the steps taken by Government to strengthen the governance capabilities of Panchayati Raj Institutions (PRIs) under the scheme, particularly through capacity building, training and digital enablement initiatives?

(a) whether the Ministry has achieved key performance milestones under Maritime India Vision (MIV) 2030, including capacity enhancement and logistics efficiency at Indian ports;
(b) if so, the year-wise improvements in key performance indicators (KPIs)  such as port capacity, vessel turnaround time and coastal cargo tonnage since 2022;
(c) the measures taken to integrate coastal States of the East Coast, including ports like Paradip, Dhamra and Gopalpur, into the strategic upgradation of coastal and inland waterway networks under MIV 2030; and
(d) whether the Ministry intends to further promote Atmanirbhar Bharat by facilitating Indian shipbuilding, maritime skill development and port-led employment generation through the Viksit Bharat Sankalp initiatives?

(a) the extent of reduction in chemical fertilizer consumption under PM-PRANAM in 2023–24 compared to the preceding three-year average and the number of States/UTs that qualified for incentive grants;
(b) the total subsidy savings accrued from this reduction and quantum disbursed to eligible States/UTs as grants up to 31 March 2025;
(c) the details of grant utilisation by March 2025, including funds used, major intervention categories and beneficiary farmers covered, State/UT-wise; and
(d) the mechanism and timeline proposed for conducting and publishing a comprehensive impact assessment of PM-PRANAM?

(a) the financial incentives and subsidies introduced to promote Zero Defect Zero Effect (ZED) certification for micro and small enterprises and the manner in which it impact, on quality and energy efficiency being tracked;
(b) whether Government is considering mandatory use of certified digital tools and cloud platforms for small businesses;
(c) if so, the details thereof;
(d) whether Government is working with the National Productivity Council to set industry-specific benchmarks; and
(e) if so, the details thereof?

