(d) the number of trainees placed in employment, internships or Startups after completion of AI-related courses?

(a) the institutional mechanisms under the  Strengthening, Upscaling & Nurturing Innovations for Livelihood (SUNIL) Programme to ensure effective participation of CBOs, SHGs and FPOs in grassroots technology delivery for EWS;
(b) whether any sector-wise evaluation has been conducted on STI interventions in health, education, natural resource management and clean energy and if so, the key findings thereof;
(c) the mechanisms to assess the long-term socio-economic impact of field-tested technologies implemented through the Land-Lab-Land model; and
(d) the extent to which the programme has contributed to enhancing S&T knowledge, skills and capacity among rural and underserved communities?

(a) whether Government is taking specific measures to address cyberbullying, online stalking and harassment of women and girls;
(b) if so, the nature of awareness campaigns, school outreach and digital literacy programmes being conducted; and
(c) whether any partnership exists between the Ministry and technology platforms to monitor and report gender-based online abuse?

(a) whether Government has undertaken initiatives to promote the adoption of digital financial tools such as mobile banking, digital lending platforms, online investment services and budgeting applications among underserved populations, if so, the details thereof;
(b) whether any specific schemes or partnerships have been launched to enhance digital financial literacy, particularly in rural and semi-urban areas and the outcomes reported so far; and
(c) whether the Ministry has identified challenges related to cybersecurity, data privacy and digital exclusion in the use of digital financial tools, if so, the measures being taken to address these challenges?

(a) the achievements and targets accomplished so far during Phase-I of biogas installations;
(b) the estimated annual CO2-equivalent reduction expected from Phase-I biogas installations and whether the Ministry has mandated standardised greenhouse gas accounting, including methane leakage measurement protocols, to track environmental performance and report under India’s NDC targets;
(c) the percentage of beneficiaries, out of the total targeted for small and medium biogas plants, who have operationalised the units;
(d) the number of rural women-led self-help groups or dairy cooperatives linked to the programme; and
(e) the specific outreach strategies implemented to promote biogas adoption in forested, hilly and tribal areas?

(a) the manner in which Government is ensuring the timely commissioning of Pumped Storage Projects (PSPs) such as Pinnapuram and Tehri, and coordinating land and water allocation with the States;
(b) the reasons behind urging States to waive local charges for PSPs, and the expected financial impact of such waivers;
